/S /H3
/P 136 0 R
/T (call may have a small call/return overhead; an optimizing compiler may inline it and remove that overhead. A macro is expanded at every use, so generated code can grow roughly with the number of uses k and the size of the replacement expression. An inline function keeps one source definition, although the compiler controls whether machine code is duplicated.)
/E (call may have a small call/return overhead; an optimizing compiler may inline it and remove that overhead. A macro is expanded at every use, so generated code can grow roughly with the number of uses k and the size of the replacement expression. An inline function keeps one source definition, although the compiler controls whether machine code is duplicated.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
>>
