<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 140 0 R
/T (takes O\(L\) time and requires O\(L\) buffer space. Direct scanf\(\) is concise but can leave invalid characters in the input stream, making recovery awkward. fgets\(\) captures the whole line, allowing the program to reject or clear the entire invalid entry before asking again. strtol\(\) also allows checking where conversion stopped and whether the value overflowed.)
/E (takes O\(L\) time and requires O\(L\) buffer space. Direct scanf\(\) is concise but can leave invalid characters in the input stream, making recovery awkward. fgets\(\) captures the whole line, allowing the program to reject or clear the entire invalid entry before asking again. strtol\(\) also allows checking where conversion stopped and whether the value overflowed.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
