896 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 149 0 R
/T (A double has a large range and is useful for scientific calculations, but decimal currency values such as 2.25 are not always represented exactly in binary floating point. It can therefore introduce small precision differences when totals are accumulated. Integer paise is preferred for billing. Both approaches need approximately constant time per addition, O\(1\), and one variable of storage, O\(1\); the main difference is exactness and overflow behaviour.)
/E (A double has a large range and is useful for scientific calculations, but decimal currency values such as 2.25 are not always represented exactly in binary floating point. It can therefore introduce small precision differences when totals are accumulated. Integer paise is preferred for billing. Both approaches need approximately constant time per addition, O\(1\), and one variable of storage, O\(1\); the main difference is exactness and overflow behaviour.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
