917 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 150 0 R
/T (The bill calculation for one household remains O\(1\) because it uses a fixed number of arithmetic operations. Processing n household bills takes O\(n\) time. A basic program can handle 800,000 bills if memory, input/output, and integer ranges are managed correctly. A production system should stream records or process batches, validate each record, log rejected records, and use checked wide-integer aggregation.)
/E (The bill calculation for one household remains O\(1\) because it uses a fixed number of arithmetic operations. Processing n household bills takes O\(n\) time. A basic program can handle 800,000 bills if memory, input/output, and integer ranges are managed correctly. A production system should stream records or process batches, validate each record, log rejected records, and use checked wide-integer aggregation.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
