919 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 150 0 R
/T (If slab limits and rates are stored in arrays and processed in a loop, the tariff function takes O\(s\) time for s slabs and O\(s\) extra space for the tariff table. With only three slabs, fixed if-statements are simple and take O\(1\) time and O\(1\) space. The array approach is easier to revise and extend to many slabs. Reading t tariff values from a configuration file takes O\(t\) start-up time and O\(t\) storage, but avoids recompilation after each approved tariff change.)
/E (If slab limits and rates are stored in arrays and processed in a loop, the tariff function takes O\(s\) time for s slabs and O\(s\) extra space for the tariff table. With only three slabs, fixed if-statements are simple and take O\(1\) time and O\(1\) space. The array approach is easier to revise and extend to many slabs. Reading t tariff values from a configuration file takes O\(t\) start-up time and O\(t\) storage, but avoids recompilation after each approved tariff change.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
