>>
endobj
946 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 151 0 R
/T (1. Read each interval record: meter ID, timestamp, and watt-hours. 2. Validate the meter ID, timestamp, and non-negative energy value. 3. Convert watt-hours to billing units \(kWh\) using 1 kWh = 1,000 Wh, retaining integer Wh internally where possible. 4. Identify whether the interval falls between 18:00 and 22:00 local time. 5. Apply the 20% peak multiplier to the energy rate for those intervals. 6. Aggregate energy charges in a sufficiently wide integer representation, with a documented rounding rule. 7. Add the fixed charge once per billing period, not once per interval. 8. Produce a bill summary and an audit trail.)
/E (1. Read each interval record: meter ID, timestamp, and watt-hours. 2. Validate the meter ID, timestamp, and non-negative energy value. 3. Convert watt-hours to billing units \(kWh\) using 1 kWh = 1,000 Wh, retaining integer Wh internally where possible. 4. Identify whether the interval falls between 18:00 and 22:00 local time. 5. Apply the 20% peak multiplier to the energy rate for those intervals. 6. Aggregate energy charges in a sufficiently wide integer representation, with a documented rounding rule. 7. Add the fixed charge once per billing period, not once per interval. 8. Produce a bill summary and an audit trail.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
