1768 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Grama JyothiRural Electricity Co-operative needs a C program to calculate the electricity bill for each household. The program uses the previous meter reading and the current meter reading to determine the electricity units consumed.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1625 0 R
>>
endobj
1769 0 obj
<<
/Title (The programcalculateselectricity consumption by comparing the previous meter reading with thecurrentmeterreading.Before performing the calculation, it checks whether both readingsarewithinthevalidrange of 0 to 65,535. When the current reading is greater than orequaltothepreviousreading, the program calculates consumption by subtracting the previousreadingfromthecurrent reading. When the current reading is smaller, the programassumesthatthemeter has completed one cycle and rolled over to zero. It then calculatestheconsumptionusing the meter range of 65,536 . For example, when the previousreadingis1200andthe current reading is 1530, the consumption is 330 units. In the rollovercase,whentheprevious reading is 65400 and the current reading is 120, the consumptionis256units.Theprogram uses constants for the maximum meter reading and meterrange,whichmakesthe code easier to understand and maintain. It also validatesuserinputtopreventinvalid meter readings from being processed.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1627 0 R
>>
endobj
