/Title (A double has a large range and is useful for scientific calculations, but decimal currency values such as 2.25 are not always represented exactly in binary floating point. It can therefore introduce small precision differences when totals are accumulated. Integer paise is preferred for billing. Both approaches need approximately constant time per addition, O\(1\), and one variable of storage, O\(1\); the main difference is exactness and overflow behaviour.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1776 0 R
>>
endobj
1847 0 obj
<<
/Title (For a small fixed tariff, symbolic constants are simple and fast. However, changing a #define value requires recompilation and redistribution. Since the co-operative expects tariff revisions, a configuration file is more suitable. At program start, the program should read the fixed charge, slab limits, rates, and effective date, validate that values are non-negative and ordered, and reject an invalid configuration. Keep a versioned backup and an audit record for every approved revision.)
/Dest [33 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1779 0 R
>>
endobj
