1853 0 obj
<<
/Title (2,102,400,000 readings for 60,000 households, and 28,032,000,000 readings for 800,000 households. The system should process records in a streaming or batched manner instead of storing all readings in memory. Processing N readings takes O\(N\) time; a streaming approach can use O\(1\) working memory per record, apart from buffers and the tariff table.)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1784 0 R
/Prev 1852 0 R
>>
endobj
