<<
/Title (For a single bill, integer paise and floating-point rupees may appear to agree for simple values. Across thousands of bills, repeated floating-point calculations can accumulate small representation errors. Integer paise gives an exact total as long as the integer type does not overflow. An int or long may be only 16 or 32 bits on some systems, so the C standard's minimum guarantees must be checked using limits.h. long long has at least 64 bits in standard C implementations that support C99 or later.)
/Dest [32 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1866 0 R
>>
endobj
